{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The new observation reproduces: A confirms leadership while a different majority elects a leader in a higher term. Submitting that successor plus the partial-repeat record."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd.pop('repeat_experiment_id',None)\n# record the successful partial-restart repeat\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['executions']['2963a0b01d97404dbf946e7b87a214f8']=[1]\npar['counterevidence'].append(\\\"Repeat receipt 2963a0b01d97404dbf946e7b87a214f8 reproduced the partial-restart outcome exactly (two restarted voters with empty configurations, the untouched voter leading at index 2 with nodes_with_full=1, then no leader among the two live voters holding log index 13 apiece; control re-electing at index 0), so the live-quorum progress loss is reproducible as well.\\\")\npar['limitations'].append(\\\"The stale-membership consequence set now includes a client-contract observation being probed: on the same stale leader, VerifyLeader returned success (leadership confirmed with the acknowledgements of itself and the promoted voter) at the very time another majority elected a leader in a higher term, so the documented protection against stale reads does not hold in that state; its retained receipt is requested in this update.\\\")\n# successor experiment carrying the new observation\nexp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_dual_majority_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"cdee42fcadd7460991a44622a9725658-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"This revision adds the client-contract observation to the same scenario: after the silent change and the acknowledged client write, the probe asks the stale-membership leader to confirm leadership (VerifyLeader) while it still leads with the promoted voter's acknowledgements, and then records whether the old majority elects a leader in a higher term in the same run. Predictions, earlier observations and comparisons are unchanged; one comparison is added for the new event.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"append_config_entry\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\",\\\"truncate_conflict\\\",\\\"vote_prevote_checks\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Same four-node scenario as the executed revision (A/B bootstrapped, A snapshots, E added as a caught-up nonvoter, C added as a voter, A restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs so its configuration is the stale {A,B}, B partitioned, AddVoter E committing the two-server change {A,B,E} on A plus E, one client command applied on A), with one addition: while A still leads on the stale membership, the probe calls VerifyLeader on A and records the result, then observes whether the old majority {B,C} elects a leader in a higher term, and emits both together.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"VerifyLeader is the documented protection clients use to avoid returning stale data from a peer that has lost leadership.\\\",\\\"The stale leader's confirmation uses the acknowledgements available to it under its in-memory configuration {A,B,E}, which is exactly the configuration its own log does not contain.\\\",\\\"The old majority's election is decided independently of the stale leader because B is partitioned from A.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No control variant: with the flag disabled the configuration is current and the two-server change cannot arise.\\\",\\\"Reads themselves are not issued; the observation is the confirmation call's result, not a data read.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"nodes\\\":4,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":300,\\\"leader_lease_timeout_ms\\\":300}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Identical to the executed revision: real bootstrap, real snapshot, real AddNonvoter catch-up, real AddVoter, real commits, graceful shutdown and restart of the leader on the same stores, real client Apply, real transport partition and real healing; the only addition is a VerifyLeader call on the stale leader between the client write and the old side's election.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_truncation2\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"silent_change\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"entry_type_at_x\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"LogConfiguration\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_fsm\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"client_write\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"write_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_verify\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_verify_pre\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_is_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"x_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_truncation2\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"committed_entry_truncated\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"An entry committed under the configuration recorded in the logs must not be replaced after the partition heals.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"x_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_fsm\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"fsm_logs_equal\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After a client write returns success, every node following the same log must apply the same committed commands.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_verify\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"x_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_verify\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"verify_confirmed_while_other_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A node must not confirm leadership for a client while a different majority of the committed configuration has elected a leader in a higher term.\\\"}\n ]\n}\nd['experiment']=exp\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
